{
 "id": "STR-06",
 "name": "pattern-slot",
 "version": 1,
 "title": "A template with a content slot",
 "summary": "One Panel template (rounded surface, muted title) used twice with different content: the template marks where content goes with patternArgument, and each call passes its own components in a patternBlock for that parameter.",
 "prompt": "Two dashboard panels in the same style: STORAGE with \"41.6 of 64 GB used\" and a usage bar, and RECENT DOWNLOADS with two files and their sizes; define the panel frame once and give each its own content.",
 "level": 3,
 "family": "STR",
 "components": [
  "ProgressBar"
 ],
 "hand_built": "The panel frame is a definePattern with a content slot because that is the lesson; the library Card is the same frame as a component, and the usage bar inside the slot is a library ProgressBar.",
 "capabilities": {
  "primary": [
   "struct.pattern_slot",
   "struct.pattern"
  ],
  "secondary": [
   "reuse.pattern",
   "layout.stack",
   "layout.decoration",
   "text.basic",
   "data.measure",
   "draw.shapes"
  ]
 },
 "use_cases": [
  "dashboard",
  "card"
 ],
 "form_factor": "square",
 "keywords": [
  "slot",
  "children",
  "content slot",
  "card template",
  "wrapper component",
  "container",
  "section",
  "panel",
  "layout template",
  "pass children"
 ],
 "teaches": [
  "Leave a hole in a template with {\"patternArgument\": {\"parameterIndex\": 1}}: parameter 1 (content) is a slot, not a value",
  "Fill the slot at the call: the call's children hold {\"patternBlock\": {\"parameterIndex\": 1, \"children\": [...]}}, any components at all",
  "Mix value parameters and slots: title is passed by name (\"title\": \"STORAGE\"), content as a block",
  "Pass a library component in a slot: the ProgressBar call inside the patternBlock is expanded there like any other node, and the template still sees only a block"
 ],
 "pitfalls": [
  "parameterIndex counts the template's parameters from 0 (title is 0, content 1); the slot parameter still has to be declared in parameters",
  "The block lands where patternArgument sits, inside the template's container: it is laid out by that column, so it is stacked, not overlaid",
  "A slot that is not given renders nothing, with no error"
 ],
 "snippets": [
  {
   "pointer": "/root/0/definePattern/children/0/column/children/2",
   "shows": "struct.pattern_slot",
   "note": "the slot: patternArgument parameterIndex 1"
  },
  {
   "pointer": "/root/1/column/children/0/Panel/children/0",
   "shows": "struct.pattern_slot",
   "note": "the call's content: patternBlock parameterIndex 1"
  },
  {
   "pointer": "/root/0",
   "shows": "struct.pattern",
   "note": "Panel template, parameters title and content"
  }
 ],
